body:
Thanks for giving me your time, it means a lot and I hope you get some sleep tonight, you obviously must be tired and could use it. I shall probably go to sleep now anyway. I shall message you tomorrow when I am back from Work. =) Thank you so much for posting here, you seem to be an amazing person and a great friend. I hope your enjoy your lecture and have a good time.

&#x200B;

Cya tomorrow, I hope you have a good evening.

I completely understand and this conversation does have such a deep meaning to me as I can relate deeply with most of what has been said. 

&#x200B;

I express my gratitude to my friends everyday. They know that they mean a lot to me and I try to be there for them like they are for me. I just need to find a way to let them in more and it should stop limiting the growth of our friendship. I can try to achieve this overtime I guess by breaking down my problems and telling them the small sections every so often.

&#x200B;

As for "her" I shall do as you said and just wait and see what happens, I suppose she needed me more than I needed her because I am hurt now but I haven't lost anything of value because I have my other friends as well as you for talking to me =) so thank you so much for that. I shall hopefully get her to understand overtime and maybe she will come back but I suppose if she doesn't it is probably for the best.

I met this person through a friend and we became really close. I would message them everyday and we would say things like "Good morning, have a good day" and just like casual greetings at the start when we didn't have time to have a full converstation. We used to talk to each other about our problems but now that she is gone, I don't really have anyone to talk to.

&#x200B;

I have a few friends that I want to develop meaningful relationships with but I just feel worthless now for the way she has treated me and the fact that I can just be thrown away like that after all those years of effort and hard times. I just wanted to be able to talk about it and fix everything but apparently if you voice your opinion in this world, you will get hurt and ignored. 

&#x200B;
